sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant A as Player A page
    participant G as Person 2 game
    participant C as Person 4 checker
    participant DB as Database via shared access
    participant B as Player B page
    A->>G: queue:join
    G-->>A: queue:status SEARCHING
    B->>G: queue:join
    G->>DB: Save match, players, private question copies
    G-->>A: match:found
    G-->>B: match:found
    A->>G: match:join
    B->>G: match:join
    G-->>A: match:snapshot
    G-->>B: match:snapshot
    loop Each shared round
        G-->>A: match:state with question and deadline
        G-->>B: match:state with question and deadline
        A->>G: match:submit with submissionId and answer
        G->>G: Check player, round, deadline, duplicate
        G->>C: Check answer against private accepted answers
        C-->>G: Correct or incorrect
        G->>DB: Save answer and marking once
        G-->>A: match:answer-received
        Note over A,B: Player B follows the same submission path
        G->>G: Close round when both answer or time ends
        G-->>A: match:round-result with marks and scores
        G-->>B: match:round-result with marks and scores
    end
    G->>DB: Save final result and lifetime totals once
    G-->>A: match:finished
    G-->>B: match:finished
    Note over A,B: Reconnect can happen during an active match
    A--xG: Connection lost
    G->>G: Start agreed grace timer; round deadline continues
    G-->>B: match:state with connection status
    A->>G: Reconnect using session cookie
    A->>G: match:resume
    G->>G: Verify identity and allowed recovery
    G-->>A: Current match:snapshot
    Note over A,B: If grace expires, apply forfeit or cancellation rules

